# Revisions that changed formatting only, so `git blame` attributes lines to the
# change that actually wrote them. Enable it once per clone:
#
#   git config blame.ignoreRevsFile .git-blame-ignore-revs
#
# Entries must be full 40-character SHAs **that exist in this repository**. Git
# errors out on an abbreviation and there is no other signal that an entry is
# bogus, so a stale SHA is invisible until someone wonders why blame stopped
# skipping. tests/test_toolchain_pin_agreement.py enforces both properties.
#
# This repository squash-merges, so a reformat's final SHA does not exist until
# its pull request lands. Add the entry in a follow-up commit on main rather
# than in the pull request doing the reformatting — a SHA recorded before the
# squash is already dead by the time anyone reads it.
